 R←Test_SendEmail_41(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕IO;⎕ML;⎕TRAP;parms;rc;msg;log;text;body;lines
⍝ Lines starting with a dot are dot-stuffed, so a single dot cannot end the message early
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 parms←∆NewMail'Created by SMTP''s ',⊃⎕SI
 body←'Line one'(,'.')'MAIL FROM:<evil@example.com>' 'RCPT TO:<victim@example.com>' 'DATA' '.leading dot' 'last line'
 parms.Body←body
 (rc msg log text)←∆Send parms
 →T.PassesIf 0=rc
 →T.PassesIf 1=+/'MAIL FROM'∘≡¨9↑¨∆SERVER.Commands
 →T.PassesIf 1=≢∆SERVER.Messages
 lines←SMTP.Message.SplitLines text
 →T.PassesIf∧/'..' '..leading dot'∊lines
 →T.PassesIf∨/body⍷SMTP.Message.SplitLines ∆Unstuff text

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
